# Documentation and workflow

Docs are part of the product. Prefer improving a canonical file over a parallel copy.

Index: `docs/README.md`.

| Need | Canonical file |
|------|----------------|
| Product architecture | `docs/architecture/overview.md` |
| Implementation snapshot | `docs/architecture.md` |
| Collector specs | `docs/collectors.md` |
| New collector workflow | `docs/development/adding-a-collector.md` |
| Data concepts | `docs/data-model/concepts.md` |
| Tables / indexes | `docs/database-model.md` |
| Testing | `docs/testing/strategy.md` |
| Local Docker ops | `docs/operations/local-development.md` |
| Durable decisions | `docs/decisions/` |

Do not document real customer access, credentials, or private infrastructure.

## ADRs

Use a light ADR (Context / Decision / Consequences / Status) only for durable material choices: history model, tenant isolation, pre-persistence exclusion, transport strategy, correlation confidence. Skip ADRs for trivial details.

## This-repo workflows (Git global rules stay in User Rules)

New collector: SPEC → transport/driver contract → synthetic parser fixtures → unit tests → persistence/correlation → API/MCP if needed → integration tests → optional lab → review.

Bug: reproduce → regression test → minimal fix → relevant integration test → docs if the contract changed.
